    "Reference CREATE remains one-shot after possible dispatch, including known 429 rejection. Complete zero/duplicate/incomplete correlation does not authorize a second POST. A rejected operation does not adopt a later matching resource. There is no resolution or supersession feature.",
    "Reference strict listing requests plain-text body representation and accepts only a real weak-or-null readback validator. HTML despite Prefer, changed candidate, invalid content, stale authority or occupied native scope cannot ACK.",
    "The complete source regression corpus and installed API authentication/HTTP smoke are separate evidence. This proof establishes no registry publication, production rollout, new Microsoft UPDATE or global source-epoch guarantee."
